\chapterpage{changes}{APPENDIX B / VISIBLE CLARIFICATIONS}{History is preserved. Status is corrected.}{These changes belong to the return delivery. Historical files are not rewritten or reused as present results.}
\begin{cols}
\subsection*{1. Contract and execution proof}
Earlier versions used ``proved'' and ``enforced'' for the general truthfulness invariant. Correctly: the rule is formulated and materialized in the project as an objective or contract. The evidence does not demonstrate universal bypass-free enforcement of all free-form statements. C04/C05 therefore distinguish model argument, normative objective and implementation evidence.

\subsection*{2. Meaning of EFFECT\_ACK}
The original prose often uses effect acknowledgement as final confirmation after the effect. The public I-D instead describes an authorization boundary before a downstream effect. Both can be useful in a larger chain but require different names and checks. This edition separates Gate-DONE and Task-DONE.

\subsection*{3. Integration theorem}
The wrapper construction states explicit assumptions. It establishes neither complete internal state preservation under lossy observation nor guaranteed arbitrary reachability. The old \code{FORMAL_PROVED} label is not adopted as current evidence without a kernel receipt.

\subsection*{4. Comparison count, time and knowledge}
99\% fewer key comparisons do not mean 99\% less total runtime. 196.4:1 is a structural ratio of historical files and selected deltas. The actual microbenchmark includes initialization and sorting. ``Provenance-bound memory'' there interprets the delta idea rather than independently measuring complete provenance validation.

\subsection*{5. Live experiment}
The earlier assertion that only one carrier remained is supplemented by the methodological finding. Existing code measures locally after download. Binary data, Git modes and the complete time boundary require correction for the stronger claim. Isolated controls document reproducible counterexamples.

\subsection*{6. The actual new parallel measurement}
PR-443 documentation at the source time contains positive 1/2/4-process results within the stated host/load scope. The earlier blanket description ``scaling open'' was incomplete for that trial. Causal explanation of earlier variation and generalization across runners remain open.

\subsection*{7. Dates and roadmap}
Earlier windows such as ``hours to one day'' are not carried forward as measurements. Access, governance, measurement correction and final fileset are explicit prerequisites. Local speedup is not transferred to physical, administrative or editorial waiting times.

\subsection*{8. Capabilities and undecidability}
The task is not represented as ``solve every solvable problem reliably and without limits''. A problem may be computable yet exceed available time, resources, observation or permissions. A universal control wrapper does not imply general semantic decidability of arbitrary programs; classical undecidability results remain relevant. \src{W7}

\begin{boundary}{Preservation without epistemic inflation}
The supplied original texts, historical microbenchmark file and layout source remain byte-identical in their source archive. The new synthesis preserves their themes while stating the source-time evidence status and clarifications. ``Every bit'' also means not quietly treating an old assertion as a present proof. English translation preserves that boundary.
\end{boundary}
\end{cols}

